### 3. **Kubernetes Logs Client**
Implement the client to fetch pod logs:

```java
import java.io.IOException;
import java.io.InputStream;
import java.net.URI;
import java.net.http.HttpClient;
import java.net.http.HttpRequest;
import java.net.http.HttpResponse;
import java.time.Duration;

public class KubernetesLogsClient {
    private final HttpClient httpClient;
    private final String apiUrl;
    private final String authToken;

    public KubernetesLogsClient() throws Exception {
        this.authToken = KubernetesConfig.getServiceAccountToken();
        this.apiUrl = KubernetesConfig.getApiServerUrl();
        this.httpClient = HttpClient.newBuilder()
                .sslContext(KubernetesConfig.getSSLContext())
                .version(HttpClient.Version.HTTP_1_1)
                .connectTimeout(Duration.ofSeconds(30))
                .build();
    }

    public String getLogs(String namespace, String podName, String container) throws IOException, InterruptedException {
        String url = String.format("%s/api/v1/namespaces/%s/pods/%s/log?container=%s",
                apiUrl, namespace, podName, container);

        HttpRequest request = HttpRequest.newBuilder()
                .uri(URI.create(url))
                .header("Authorization", "Bearer " + authToken)
                .GET()
                .build();

        HttpResponse<String> response = httpClient.send(request, HttpResponse.BodyHandlers.ofString());

        if (response.statusCode() >= 400) {
            throw new IOException("Failed to fetch logs: " + response.body());
        }

        return response.body();
    }

    public InputStream streamLogs(String namespace, String podName, String container, boolean follow)
            throws IOException, InterruptedException {
        String url = String.format("%s/api/v1/namespaces/%s/pods/%s/log?container=%s&follow=%s",
                apiUrl, namespace, podName, container, follow);

        HttpRequest request = HttpRequest.newBuilder()
                .uri(URI.create(url))
                .header("Authorization", "Bearer " + authToken)
                .GET()
                .build();

        HttpResponse<InputStream> response = httpClient.send(request, HttpResponse.BodyHandlers.ofInputStream());

        if (response.statusCode() >= 400) {
            throw new IOException("Failed to stream logs: " + new String(response.body().readAllBytes()));
        }

        return response.body();
    }
}
```

### 4. **Usage Example**
Fetch and stream logs from a pod:

```java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        KubernetesLogsClient client = new KubernetesLogsClient();

        // Fetch logs once
        String logs = client.getLogs("default", "my-pod", "my-container");
        System.out.println(logs);

        // Stream logs continuously
        try (InputStream logStream = client.streamLogs("default", "my-pod", "my-container", true)) {
            byte[] buffer = new byte[1024];
            int bytesRead;
            while ((bytesRead = logStream.read(buffer)) != -1) {
                System.out.print(new String(buffer, 0, bytesRead));
            }
        }
    }
}
```

### 5. **Error Handling**
- **Authentication Errors**: Ensure the service account has permission to read logs (configure RBAC).
- **Network Errors**: Handle `IOException` for connection issues.
- **HTTP Errors**: Check status codes (e.g., 404 for missing pods).

