To download a page directly from the browser console using its URL, you can use JavaScript's `fetch` API and create a downloadable link. Here's how to do it:

### Step-by-Step Code:
1. **Open the Browser Console**:  
   Press `F12` (or `Ctrl+Shift+J`/`Cmd+Option+J`) to open the developer tools and navigate to the **Console** tab.

2. **Run the Script**:  
   Copy and paste the following code into the console. Replace `https://example.com` with your target URL.

   ```javascript
   (async function() {
     const url = 'https://example.com'; // Replace with your URL
     try {
       // Fetch the page content
       const response = await fetch(url);
       const content = await response.text();

       // Create a download link
       const blob = new Blob([content], { type: 'text/plain' });
       const downloadUrl = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
       const link = document.createElement('a');
       link.href = downloadUrl;
       link.download = 'downloaded-page.html'; // Filename for the downloaded file
       document.body.appendChild(link);
       link.click();

       // Cleanup
       document.body.removeChild(link);
       URL.revokeObjectURL(downloadUrl);
       console.log('Download started!');
     } catch (error) {
       console.error('Error:', error);
     }
   })();
